^warning: ignoring
approximating inline assembly statement at .* line (19|53|54) function main
--
A memory access at an address that may depend on a value CBMC does not model
(here: registers the statement does not initialise, or a system register read
by mrs) would change no object, as CBMC cannot relate such an address to an
object. Such statements are approximated. The assertions that fail may be violated
on hardware (x or y is then changed); the others hold on hardware.
